  specialized scenarios where there's not  a ton of data right where you don't  you're not really latency sensitive and  where you do have this scenario where  you want two parties who  are like they want to be able to compute  something together right but they don't  fully trust each other to actually be  able to use this technology and we  actually do have some experimental  projects which do stuff like that a good  example of the kind of thing you with  this is what's called secure set  intersection that's where like let's say  that you know you have a bunch of users  and I have a bunch of users that are  doing something and we want to know like  which of them are in common right but we  neither of us wants to reveal our full  user list to the other one right so this  would allow us to compute something like  that for example right and maybe we're  okay if it takes a little while right  it's not really big deal of it takes a  while so along those lines actually  bigquery has built some experimental  support for doing queries on encrypted  data which basically lets you like  upload encrypted data so that like  bigquery itself can't see it yet  bigquery is able to run some queries  forgive you back some answers that will  actually like answer your query in a way  that bakery never saw either the actual  question in some cases with some caveats  or the data itself which is pretty cool  it's not super scale but it is something  that is out there and you can actually  play with it on github cool that sounds  like the feature very interesting well  we're we're definitely running out of  time but just very quickly is there  anything else we might have missed or  you need to plug or resources people  should go look at I think probably the  best thing to do if you're really  interested in this topic is to check out  the encryption white paper that we  recently put out has a ton of detail  unlike how this stuff works we can also  put up a link to the encrypted bigquery  cl